From: Salty <99386653+PjSalty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 08:41:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] startup: raise the thread-pool worker floor in code

Intent: the 2026-08-27 stall had the pool's worker floor at the core
count while EF cache writes blocked synchronously on Redis: bursts
queued API work behind the pool's one-to-two threads per second ramp,
p95 hit five seconds and webOS clients timed out. The env knob was
already deployed and did nothing: DOTNET_ThreadPool_MinThreads=32 was
ignored without a word. Raise the floor to max(32, current) in code
instead, completion-port floor untouched, and log the before and after
values at Information: "worker floor raised" greppable from the pod log
is the contract that the floor is real. 32 is the 2026-08-29 load
measurement. It runs in every startup mode, the migration Job included.
Carried onto 12.x (.NET 10) with one change: the method is now
EnsureThreadPoolFloor, because a Raise* name trips CA1030 ("use events")
in Debug builds on the 12.x analyzer set. 12.x item code is still
largely synchronous EF, so a burst still blocks pool threads per round
trip.
Ceiling: a forced runtime floor (runtimeconfig
System.Threading.ThreadPool.MinThreads or its environment twin) makes
SetMinThreads refuse any other value; the Warning line then replaces
the Information line, which the smoke assertion catches.
Drop when: the runtime raises its default floor above the core count or
logs the effective floor, or upstream sets the floor itself.

Patch: 0015
---
 Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs                |  1 +
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs b/Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs
index 93c9961..210832a 100644
--- a/Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs
+++ b/Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ using System.Linq;
 using System.Runtime.InteropServices;
 using System.Runtime.Versioning;
 using System.Text;
+using System.Threading;
 using System.Threading.Tasks;
 using Emby.Server.Implementations;
 using Jellyfin.Server.ServerSetupApp;
@@ -297,4 +298,31 @@ public static class StartupHelpers
         // Ref: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.text.codepagesencodingprovider.instance?view=netcore-3.0#remarks
         Encoding.RegisterProvider(CodePagesEncodingProvider.Instance);
     }
+
+    /// <summary>
+    /// Raises the worker-thread floor of the managed thread pool.
+    /// </summary>
+    /// <param name="logger">The logger to use.</param>
+    public static void EnsureThreadPoolFloor(ILogger logger)
+    {
+        // DOTNET_ThreadPool_MinThreads was in place and silently ignored: the
+        // runtime gives no feedback when it drops a config knob, and the
+        // DOTNET_/COMPlus_ family parses numbers as hex on top of that. With the
+        // floor stuck at the core count, a burst of synchronous cache writes
+        // queued API work behind the pool's one-to-two threads per second ramp
+        // until clients timed out. Set the floor in code and log it; the log
+        // line below is the proof the floor is real. 32 is the 2026-08-29 load
+        // measurement, and the current values win when they are already higher.
+        const int MinimumWorkerThreads = 32;
+        ThreadPool.GetMinThreads(out var workerThreads, out var completionPortThreads);
+        var targetWorkerThreads = Math.Max(MinimumWorkerThreads, workerThreads);
+        if (ThreadPool.SetMinThreads(targetWorkerThreads, completionPortThreads))
+        {
+            logger.LogInformation("Thread pool worker floor raised: {PreviousWorkerThreads} -> {TargetWorkerThreads}", workerThreads, targetWorkerThreads);
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            logger.LogWarning("Thread pool worker floor raise rejected by the runtime: {PreviousWorkerThreads} -> {TargetWorkerThreads}", workerThreads, targetWorkerThreads);
+        }
+    }
 }
diff --git a/Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs b/Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs
index 715fc3d..50fc05d 100644
--- a/Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs
+++ b/Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs
@@ -115,6 +115,7 @@ namespace Jellyfin.Server
                 Assembly.GetEntryAssembly()!.GetName().Version!.ToString(3));
 
             StartupHelpers.LogEnvironmentInfo(_logger, appPaths);
+            StartupHelpers.EnsureThreadPoolFloor(_logger);
 
             // If hosting the web client, validate the client content path
             if (startupConfig.HostWebClient())
